From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:56:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 182/209] feat(area): click-click-double-click creation of a
 polygon shape

"Create Object -> Area -> Polygon" now draws a shape the way EditorQt does
(CShapeObject::MouseCreateCallback, ShapeObject.cpp:1155-1237) instead of
placing a default-sized one.

CShapeCreateTool, registered as "EditTool.AreaShapeCreate", is what the new
CAreaShapePolygonClassDesc returns from GetToolClassName(), so the Create panel
starts it instead of the generic CObjectCreateTool
(ObjectCreateToolPanel.cpp:383-402) - the route CryDesigner's AreaSolid entry
takes. The first click spawns the entity with its CPolygonShapeComponent at the
point under the cursor (terrain and geometry pick, grid snapped) and makes that
the shape's first point; every further click appends one; a double-click or
Enter finishes; Esc, or fewer than three points, deletes the entity again. The
whole creation is one undo step, and the finished entity is selected.

While drawing, the tool draws the committed edges plus a rubber band from the
last point to the cursor and a faint closing edge, so the polygon reads before
it exists. The click that opens a double click lands on the same pixel as the
double click, so a point within a centimetre of the previous one is dropped -
that is what legacy achieves by popping its trailing temporary point.

The Box entry is left on the standard single-click placement: click-drag sizing
would need a second tool class (the Create panel passes a tool no user data, so
one tool serves exactly one class), and a legacy AreaBox is placed the same way.

